[[0,67799,0,12,0,12,"2015-03-22T22:56:01","european","",[],"","how reddit grew","http://motherboard.vice.com/read/how-reddit-got-huge-tons-of-fake-accounts--2","random"],[1,102664,0,2,0,2,"2015-03-22T23:55:02","Xseleon","",[],"<p>I wonder how common this must be. I recently read a <a href=\"http://hypebot.com/hypebot/2014/10/read-the-email-from-groovesharks-co-founder-that-lost-a-lawsuit-and-doomed-his-company.html\">similar article</a> for the music streaming site grooveshark, that did something similar. Instead of making a massive number of accounts, they asked people to seed the site by uploading songs, legal and otherwise.</p>"],[1,128913,0,0,0,0,"2015-04-10T02:35:45","Vercingetorix","",[],"<p>So it was bullshit from the start. Can't say I'm surprised.</p>"]]